To maintain this code properly, the following repositories have to be
tracked for changes (maintenance details below):

- https://github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3
- https://github.com/sqlcipher/sqlcipher
- https://github.com/libtom/libtomcrypt
- https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls (only library/aesce.c, see below)

Run ./check_upstream.sh to see which of them have newer versions.


Update code from https://github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3
----------------------------------------------------

Current release: v1.14.53

1. git clone mattn/go-sqlite3 new version to temp dir
2. ./track_go-sqlite3.sh <mattn/go-sqlite3 dir>
   (copies Go files and _example, rewrites import paths, and lists Go files
   that upstream does not have: delete the ones upstream removed/renamed,
   keep the local ones: flags.go, sqlcipher.go, sqlcipher_test.go,
   crypto_check.go, crypto_test.go, sqlite3_opt_json1.go)
3. Re-apply to sqlite3.go:
   - #include <stdint.h> after #include <string.h> in the C preamble
   - `var cipherPragmas []string` with the other DSN variables in Open
   - `cipherPragmas, err = parseCipherPragmas(params)` after the vfs param
   - execute cipherPragmas right after the `exec` helper is defined, before
     "Busy timeout" (PRAGMA key MUST run before all other statements)
4. Update the version in this file and in README.md


Update code from https://github.com/sqlcipher/sqlcipher
-------------------------------------------------------

Current release: v4.20.0 (SQLite 3.54.1)

Note:
v4.14.0 restored LibTomCrypt support (it was removed in v4.12.0).
If a future version removes it again, revert the corresponding commit
(see https://github.com/sqlcipher/sqlcipher/issues/564).
SQLCipher 5.x is not compatible with 4.x databases by default.

Execute:
1. git clone sqlcipher to temp dir
2. git checkout v4.20.0
3. ./configure --with-tempstore=yes \
     CFLAGS="-DSQLITE_HAS_CODEC \
             -DSQLITE_EXTRA_INIT=sqlcipher_extra_init \
             -DSQLITE_EXTRA_SHUTDOWN=sqlcipher_extra_shutdown \
             -DSQLCIPHER_CRYPTO_LIBTOMCRYPT"
4. make sqlite3.c
5. Copy sqlite3.c and sqlite3.h
6. Check for compiler warnings (gcc and clang, -Wall) with the cgo flags from
   flags.go. Since v4.20.0 none need patching; older releases needed (char*)
   casts where strrchr()/strchr() results were assigned to non-const.


Update code from https://github.com/libtom/libtomcrypt
------------------------------------------------------

Current HEAD: 6c6d5104de66f3ca0dfd7b68540ef86869982b07
(from develop branch, 2026-09-01)

Note: the last official release is v1.18.2 (2018); all development happens
on the develop branch.

./track_libtomcrypt.sh <libtomcrypt dir>
copies the files, makes aes.c include aes_tab.h instead of aes_tab.c and
applies patches/aes_desc_armce.patch (ARMv8 AES dispatch, see below).

Hardware acceleration is LibTomCrypt's own runtime detection (do not define
LTC_NO_ASM or LTC_NO_ACCEL in flags.go):
- x86/x86_64: AES-NI (aesni.c), SHA extensions (sha*_x86.c)
- aarch64: ARMv8 Crypto Extensions AES via aes_armce.c (go-sqlcipher)
Defining LTC_NO_ACCEL (e.g. CGO_CFLAGS=-DLTC_NO_ACCEL) forces the portable C
implementations; CI tests that configuration.


ARMv8 AES (aes_armce.c, aes_armce.h, patches/aes_desc_armce.patch)
------------------------------------------------------------------

Not from any upstream: glue that lets LibTomCrypt's aes_desc use the ARMv8
Cryptography Extensions on aarch64, mirroring its AES-NI dispatch. The round
function, key expansion and inverse key schedule are derived from Mbed TLS
3.6.7 library/aesce.c. When Mbed TLS releases a new 3.6.x, check
git log mbedtls-3.6.7..mbedtls-3.6.N -- library/aesce.c
for fixes relevant to these parts. crypto_test.go cross-checks the result
against the portable implementation (CI runs it on arm64 Linux and macOS).
